{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.QSubstrate","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_stab_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_stab_pos","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L384-L395","doc":"**Stabilisation preserves the sign of the Markov trace.**  Scaling\nby the strictly positive Markov parameter cannot flip or kill a\npositive trace.\n\nThis is the content the `∀ (z : ℝ)` binder destroyed: with `z`\nuniversally quantified the trace was identically zero, so no `x`\nsatisfied the hypothesis and the statement said nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovParameter_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovParameter_pos","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L376-L382","doc":"The Markov parameter `z = 1 / (q_0^{1/2} + q_0^{-1/2})` is strictly\npositive: `q_0 > 1 > 0`, so both `rpow` terms are positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_zero","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L360-L367","doc":"**Trace of the zero element is zero** — derived from\nhomogeneity via `0 • x = 0` and `markovTrace_smul`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_smul","kind":"theorem","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L348-L358","doc":"**Trace of a scaled element** scales by the same factor.\n\n**Theorem** (was previously `axiom markovTrace_smul`).\nDischarged 2026-06-08: derived from `markovTrace_linear`'s\n`map_smul` field, with the `c • r = c * r` identity for\n`r : ℝ` (via `smul_eq_mul`). Term-mode proof for faster\nelaboration (per gemini-code-assist review on PR #1986). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_add","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L333-L346","doc":"**Trace of an additive sum** distributes.\n\n**Theorem** (was previously `axiom markovTrace_add`).\nDischarged 2026-06-08: derived from the stronger\n`markovTrace_linear` axiom (which carries both `map_add` and\n`map_smul` via `IsLinearMap`). Net: this file shrinks by 2\naxioms (this `markovTrace_add` and the sibling\n`markovTrace_smul` below — both derive from `map_add` /\n`map_smul` of the upstream `markovTrace_linear`); the\nlinearity claim is concentrated in the single\n`markovTrace_linear` axiom upstream. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.wenzlBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.wenzlBridge","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L305-L331","doc":"**Wenzl bridge** (categorical identity): the Markov trace\nof an element via its Wedderburn decomposition equals the\nweighted sum of block traces.\n\n`tr_M(x) = Σ_{λ ⊢ n} y_λ(q) · tr(x λ)`\n\nwhere `tr` is the ordinary matrix trace per block.  This is\nthe categorical content that the Python compute layer\nimplements in `wedderburn_jones_markov.py`.\n\n**The `q` is `QSubstrate.q_0`, not a `∀`-bound variable.**  It used\nto be universally quantified, which is the same defect as in\n`MarkovTrace_markov_axiom` above and equally corrosive here:\n`markovTraceOnWedderburn x` does not mention `q`, so a `∀ q` on the\nright makes the weighted block-sum *provably independent of `q`*\n(`wenzlBridge_q_independent_defect` below, which no longer\ntypechecks against this corrected statement).  The `q`-dependence of\n`y_λ(q)` is the entire content of the Wenzl bridge, so the old form\nasserted the negation of what it was for.  `WedderburnDecomposition`\nis defined as the decomposition of `H_n(q_0)` (see\n`Wedderburn.lean`), so `q_0` is the only `q` the statement can\nhonestly mean.  Bean `qou-ck1f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTraceOnWedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTraceOnWedderburn","kind":"def","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L293-L303","doc":"**Categorical Markov trace on a Wedderburn decomposition**\n(axiomatised) — the categorical-level Markov trace `tr_M`\napplied directly to a `WedderburnDecomposition n`.  Bridges\nthe gap between the abstract `markovTrace : HeckeElement n →\nℝ` (vector form) and the per-block decomposition.  The\n`wenzlBridge` below relates this trace to the block-trace\nsum form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markov_axioms_vacuous_of_weight_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markov_axioms_vacuous_of_weight_zero","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L265-L291","doc":"**Both trace properties hold automatically under a zero weight.**\n\nSo neither imposes a constraint that rules out the degenerate trace:\ncyclicity becomes `0 = 0` and the Markov property becomes `0 = z * 0`.\n\n\"Properties\", not \"axioms\", as of 2026-08-26: cyclicity is **no longer an\naxiom here** — it was removed as a zero-consumer assumption (see the\n§Cyclicity note above), so the first conjunct is now an ordinary statement\nthis lemma shows is satisfiable rather than one the module assumes.\n`MarkovTrace_markov_axiom` is still an axiom, and the second conjunct is\nstill about it.\n\nThis is the sharp form of the warning in `markovTrace`'s docstring, and it is\nthe residue of bean `qou-ck1f`: that bean removed a `∀ (z : ℝ)` binder which\n*proved* `tr_M ≡ 0`. Removing it removed the proof of degeneracy. Nothing was\nadded that excludes it, and this lemma is what makes that concrete. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_eq_zero_of_weight_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_eq_zero_of_weight_zero","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L259-L263","doc":"A zero Riesz weight collapses the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.MarkovTrace_markov_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.MarkovTrace_markov_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L218-L244","doc":"**Markov axiom** for the Markov trace: stabilisation scales\nthe trace by *the* Markov parameter\n`z = 1 / (q_0^{1/2} + q_0^{-1/2})` — the single constant\n`QSubstrate.markovParameter`, not an arbitrary real:\n\n`tr_M(stab_n x) = z · tr_M(x)`.\n\n**The `z` used to be a `∀`-bound variable, which made this axiom\ncollapse the Markov trace to zero.**  With `∀ (z : ℝ)` in front,\ninstantiating at `z = 0` and `z = 1` gives\n\n    markovTrace (n+1) (heckeStab x) = 0        (z := 0)\n    markovTrace (n+1) (heckeStab x) = markovTrace n x   (z := 1)\n\nhence `markovTrace n x = 0` for *every* `n` and *every* `x`.  The\ncorpus stayed consistent — the zero map satisfies\n`markovTrace_linear`, the only other constraint on `markovTrace` —\nbut `tr_M`, the central object of the mass chain\n`M = ρ · m_e · |tr_M(T_w)|`, was pinned to the zero function, so\nevery downstream statement about it was vacuously about `0`.\nThe docstring already said \"z := QSubstrate.markovParameter\"; only\nthe binder was wrong.  Bean `qou-ck1f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.heckeStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.heckeStab","kind":"opaque","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L210-L216","doc":"**Stabilisation map** `stab_n : HeckeElement n → HeckeElement\n(n + 1)` corresponding to multiplication by the generator\n`σ_n`.  Axiomatised pending the concrete construction\n(which requires the Hecke generator `σ_n` to be expressible\nas a `HeckeElement (n + 1)` — the natural inclusion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.«term_*_h_»","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.«term_*_h_»","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L168-L169","doc":"Notation for Hecke-algebra multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.heckeMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.heckeMul","kind":"opaque","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L152-L166","doc":"**Hecke-algebra multiplication**, carried opaquely.\n\nAn `opaque` definition is a datum: it adds nothing to the assumption surface\n(no `axiom`), it merely declines to say what the operation is. The concrete\nmultiplication is the matrix algebra under the Wedderburn embedding\n(`QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn.blockDiagonal`, and `wedderburnEmbedOf` for\nthe `Fin (heckeDim n)` landing), via the Hoefsmit representation in\n`QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Hoefsmit`.  This pointed at `wedderburnEmbed` until that\n`opaque` was deleted on 2026-09-05; the target is now a real construction.\n\nKept — unlike the cyclicity axiom that used to accompany it, see below —\nbecause `markov_axioms_vacuous_of_weight_zero` needs a multiplication to state\nwhat the removed axiom would have constrained. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.partitions_as_finset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.partitions_as_finset","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L105-L115","doc":"The Jones-Markov coefficients `y_λ(q)` are real-valued and\nsum to 1 across partitions: `Σ_{λ ⊢ n} y_λ(q) = 1` (the\ncentral-element normalisation, per Wenzl 1988 Lemma 3.2).\n\nStated against an explicit `Finset` of partitions\n(`partitions_as_finset n`) since `Nat.Partition n` is a\nproposition, not a `Finset`.  CLOSED: Mathlib provides\n`Fintype (Nat.Partition n)` in `Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition`,\nso we can use `Finset.univ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.jonesMarkovCoefficient_eq_wenzlClosedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.jonesMarkovCoefficient_eq_wenzlClosedForm","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L88-L103","doc":"**Identification** (Wenzl 1988 Lemma 3.2): the abstract Jones-Markov\ncoefficient IS the Wenzl closed form.\n\nDefinitional, hence `rfl` — `JonesMarkovCoefficient` is defined as\n`wenzlClosedForm` directly above. Recorded as a named theorem anyway,\nbecause until 2026-08-25 this was an `axiom` in\n`QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovWenzl` and a reader looking for it there will\nnow find only a comment. Stating it here also means a future refactor that\nmakes `JonesMarkovCoefficient` something other than `wenzlClosedForm`\nbreaks a theorem rather than silently changing what the corpus means by\n`y_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.JonesMarkovCoefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace.JonesMarkovCoefficient","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/MarkovTrace.lean#L81-L86","doc":"**Jones-Markov central coefficient** `y_λ(q)` for partition\n`λ` at parameter `q`.  Axiomatised; concrete Wenzl 1988 §3\nformula is deferred to the next round of Lean port. ","signatureChunk":0}]}